{
 "stop": [
  {
   "letter": "S",
   "word": "Stop",
   "text": "Stop moving and sit down if you can. Take a few slow breaths. Panic makes people rush and make mistakes; a few calm minutes now costs you nothing."
  },
  {
   "letter": "T",
   "word": "Think",
   "text": "What do you have with you: in your pockets, your bag, your vehicle? What do you already know how to do? Does anyone know where you are? A clear head is your best tool."
  },
  {
   "letter": "O",
   "word": "Observe",
   "text": "Look around. Where could you find shelter, water and firewood? What is the weather doing, and how much daylight is left? Watch for hazards such as fast water, steep ground, smoke or traffic. Is anyone with you hurt?"
  },
  {
   "letter": "P",
   "word": "Plan",
   "text": "Decide what matters most and do it in order: injuries first, then staying warm and dry, then water, then getting found. Food can wait longer than you think. Pick the step below that fits right now."
  }
 ],
